questions.question:
Which of the following is NOT an infinite loop?
(A) for (i = 100; i < 500; --i) { }
(B) while(1) { }
(C) i = 10; for (i < 20; ++i) { }
(D) for (i = 10; i < 20; --i) { i = i - 2; }

What is the output of the following code?
main() {
    int i = 1;
    while(1) {
        printf("%d\n", i++);
        if(i > 10)
            break;
    }
}

How many times will the inner loop body execute in the following?
for(i=1; i<=3; i++)
    for(j=1; j<=4; j++)
        printf("*");
